  "verbalization": "Vidalol B is consistently linked to SNU-387, which is identified as the target of multiple compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion. All these compounds ultimately have KB as their target. This suggests that Vidalol B may exert its effects through a common mechanism that targets SNU-387, which is a key molecule in the pathway leading to KB. The evidence points to a potential interaction where Vidalol B influences SNU-387, which in turn affects KB. The recurring involvement of SNU-387 as a target of multiple compounds implies that it may be a central mediator in the relationship between Vidalol B and KB. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on SNU-387, which could be a critical node in the biological process that connects Vidalol B to KB.",
